        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.154,
                0.178,
                0.844,
                0.214
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "Uganda: Report on Rebasing of Monthly Indicator of Economic Growth (July 7–18, 2025)\nPrepared by Anthony Silungwe",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.112,
                0.233,
                0.836,
                0.286
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "The High-Level Summary Technical Assistance Report series provides high-level summaries of the assistance provided to IMF capacity development recipients, describing the high-level objectives, findings, and recommendations.",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.112,
                0.305,
                0.876,
                0.505
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "ABSTRACT: This capacity development (CD) project, financed by the Data for Decisions (D4D) Fund,\\(^{1}\\) was initiated in response to a request from the Ghana Statistical Service (GSS) to provide technical assistance (TA) on developing a Monthly Indicator of Economic Growth (MIEG). The project aimed to establish a robust MIEG compilation framework aligned with the International Monetary Fund's Quarterly National Accounts Manual (2017), enhancing timeliness and quality of economic statistics. Key findings include the successful creation of a Value Added Tax (VAT) database critical for compiling both MIEG and quarterly GDP estimates, alongside training on data cleaning tools that improve data accuracy. The project revealed some discrepancies between MIEG and quarterly GDP figures, highlighting the need for harmonization. Recommendations focus on the phased adoption of the new VAT processing files, timely dissemination of experimental MIEG data, and closer integration of MIEG with quarterly GDP compilation to improve consistency and statistical quality.",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.122,
                0.528,
                0.482,
                0.546
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "JEL Classification Numbers: J01, J16, J30, E001",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.121,
                0.557,
                0.804,
                0.592
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "Keywords: Monthly Indicator of Economic Growth (MIEG), Index of Industrial Production (IIP), manufacturing, Value Added Tax (VAT) data, National Accounts.",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.112,
                0.628,
                0.882,
                0.718
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "The contents of this document constitute a high-level summary of technical advice provided by the staff of the International Monetary Fund (IMF) to the authorities of a member country or international agency (the \"CD recipient\") in response to their request for capacity development. Unless the CD recipient specifically objects within 30 business days of its transmittal, the IMF will publish this high-level summary on IMF.org (see Staff Operational Guidance on the Dissemination of Capacity Development Information \\( ^{2} \\) ).",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.322,
                0.732,
                0.675,
                0.823
            ],
